<task id="016" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Channel seams — define `ICommunicationChannelSender` + `ICommunicationArchiver` (email is the only R4 impl)</title>
    <phase>Wave 1 — Server: enrichment + deterministic engine</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>5</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>005</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, architecture</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Introduces two channel-extensibility seam interfaces + refactors the existing email send/archive into the first implementations behind them; establishes the NFR-04 "no-change-to-add-a-channel" boundary; respects ADR-010 / ADR-045 + bff-extensions governance.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-seams</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>NFR-04</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    DEFINE (not fully implement for other channels) the two channel-extensibility seams that let future channels plug in without touching the engine, enrichment, regarding model, or review UI (NFR-04):

    • **`ICommunicationChannelSender`** — dispatch `SendAsync` by `CommunicationType`; the EMAIL implementation wraps the existing Graph send path in `CommunicationService`.
    • **`ICommunicationArchiver`** — `GenerateEml`/archive; the EMAIL implementation wraps the existing `.eml` generation (`EmlGenerationService`/`GraphMessageToEmlConverter`).

    Email is the ONLY R4 implementation of each. The seams must be shaped so that adding a channel = adding a new sender/archiver adapter + a normalizer to the envelope — the Association Engine, `ICommunicationEnrichmentService`, the regarding model, and the review UI MUST NOT change to add a channel. Do NOT build Teams/Slack/Gmail/SMS code (MUST NOT per project rules). Provide the interfaces, an email impl behind each, and a `CommunicationType`-keyed dispatch/registration that resolves the email impl today and is ready for more later.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF architect for the Communication subsystem. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-010 (DI minimalism via `CommunicationModule`), ADR-045 (Communication ADR — channel seams), NFR-04 (channel extensibility), §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `ICommunicationChannelSender` (dispatch by `CommunicationType`) and `ICommunicationArchiver` (`GenerateEml`/archive) exist, with a single email implementation behind each wrapping the current Graph send + `.eml` generation. A `CommunicationType`-keyed dispatch resolves the email sender/archiver. The engine, enrichment, regarding model, and review surface are unchanged by (and would remain unchanged for) a future channel. Build clean; seam + dispatch tests pass; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R4 ships ONLY the email channel but must be channel-extensible by construction (NFR-04, DEC-11). Today, send and `.eml` archival are email-specific code inside `CommunicationService` + `EmlGenerationService`/`GraphMessageToEmlConverter`. This task hoists them behind two seams so the rest of the intelligence layer is channel-agnostic — the Association Engine already operates over the normalized envelope (task 011), so the remaining channel-specific surfaces are exactly "send" and "archive," which these two interfaces isolate.

      Component Justification (§11): the two new interfaces are justified because the concrete failure mode without them is that adding any future channel forces edits into the engine/enrichment/regarding/review surfaces (violating NFR-04) — the seams are the boundary that prevents that. Cost-of-doing-nothing is a named contract failure (NFR-04), not "future flexibility."

      Scope discipline: this is seams + email impl ONLY. No Teams/Slack/Gmail/SMS implementations (explicit MUST NOT). Keep the email impls as thin wrappers over existing, working code — behavior for email must be unchanged.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/EmlGenerationService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/GraphMessageToEmlConverter.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationType.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Define (not implement other channels) `ICommunicationChannelSender` + `ICommunicationArchiver`; email is the only R4 impl. Association Engine, enrichment service, regarding model, and review UI MUST NOT change to add a future channel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT build Teams/Slack/Gmail/SMS channel code — seams only (DEC-11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Email impls are thin wrappers over the existing Graph send + `.eml` generation; email behavior unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Dispatch keyed by `CommunicationType`; the email impl resolves for the email type today; registration is ready for more channels without engine changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register seams + email impls via `CommunicationModule` only; keep DI unconditional (ADR-032).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Channel seams are codified in ADR-045 (task 005); confirm the interface shapes match the ADR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 Component Justification: state the concrete NFR-04 failure mode prevented by each new interface in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
