    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Type-keyed dispatch" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs">
        Resolve the sender/archiver by `CommunicationType`; email resolves the Graph impl. New channel = new keyed registration, no dispatch-site change.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Thin adapter over working code" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/EmlGenerationService.cs">
        Wrap the existing `.eml` generation behind `ICommunicationArchiver` without altering its behavior.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `CommunicationService.cs` (Graph send path) + `EmlGenerationService.cs`/`GraphMessageToEmlConverter.cs` (`.eml` generation) + `CommunicationType.cs` to identify the exact email-specific surfaces to isolate.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F + §11 Component Justification + the ADR-045 channel-seam section before defining interfaces.</step>
    <step order="3">Define `ICommunicationChannelSender` (`Task&lt;...&gt; SendAsync(...)`, plus a `CommunicationType SupportedType` or equivalent for keyed dispatch) and `ICommunicationArchiver` (`GenerateEml`/archive) in `Services/Communication/`.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement `EmailChannelSender` wrapping the existing Graph send in `CommunicationService`, and `EmailArchiver` wrapping `.eml` generation — thin adapters, email behavior unchanged.</step>
    <step order="5">Add `CommunicationType`-keyed dispatch (a small resolver/factory or keyed DI) that returns the email impl for the email type; shape it so a future channel is a new registration, not a dispatch-site edit.</step>
    <step order="6">Refactor `CommunicationService` send + archive call sites to route through the seams (email path only). Confirm the Association Engine / enrichment / regarding / review surfaces are untouched.</step>
    <step order="7">Register seams + email impls + dispatch in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional.</step>
    <step order="8">Write tests: email send routes through `ICommunicationChannelSender`; `.eml` archive routes through `ICommunicationArchiver`; dispatch resolves the email impl by `CommunicationType`; a fake second channel type could register without touching the dispatch site (extensibility assertion).</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing send/archive tests still pass (email behavior unchanged).</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/r4-016-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus NFR-04 seam boundary + §11 justification + ADR-010). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (016 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (interface shapes, dispatch mechanism, keyed-DI vs factory).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
