  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`ICommunicationChannelSender` and `ICommunicationArchiver` interfaces exist in `Services/Communication/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Exactly one implementation of each exists (email); no Teams/Slack/Gmail/SMS code is present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Email send routes through `ICommunicationChannelSender`; `.eml` archival routes through `ICommunicationArchiver`; email behavior is unchanged (existing tests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dispatch resolves the email impl by `CommunicationType`; a test shows a second channel type could register without editing the dispatch site (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Association Engine, `ICommunicationEnrichmentService`, regarding model, and review surface are untouched by this task (grep/diff-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seams + impls registered via `CommunicationModule`, unconditional.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta ≈ 0; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends only on ADR-045 (task 005) for the interface shapes; can run any time after 005 (not on the 010→011→rungs→015 serial spine). `blocks` is empty — it is an independent W1 seam task.

    Strict scope: seams + email impl only. If a future-channel need seems to demand an engine/enrichment change, that is a signal the seam is mis-shaped — fix the seam, do not leak channel specifics into the engine (NFR-04). No new-channel implementation code (MUST NOT).

    W7 add-in work and W2 client send both continue to call the BFF send endpoint; this task is server-internal refactoring behind that endpoint — the send contract is unchanged.
  </notes>

